<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc launches new insecticide.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc launches new insecticide.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rhodic, a 100 percent owned subsidiary of Rhone-Poulenc Agro, said Tuesday it is launching a new insecticide in France and Germany aimed at the cockroach control market.</p>
<p>The company said GOLIATH Gel is odorless and may be used at any time of day, without disturbing the inhabitants of the building undergoing treatment.</p>
<p>These advantages, the company said, will make GOLIATH Gel an excellent replacement for spray treatments.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Agro is a unit of Rhone-Poulenc Inc, the U.S. unit of Rhone-Poulenc SA.</p>
</text>
